=== NIO ===
More complete, flexible and safer than File

== Path ==
Interface which replaces the class File
+ Represents the path of the file
+ You can navigate, observe, compare paths of files using your methods

== Paths ==
A utility class which offers methods to create objects from Path
+ Paths.get(value) -> converts a string to a Path object

= Absolute Path =
Complete localization of the file/directory from the root of system
Windows -> C:\Users\Renzo\Docs\file.txt
Linux -> /home/users/folder/file.txt

= Relative Path =
Localization based on the actual directory, don't start from root, but with "." or ".." (based on context of exec)
folder/file.txt
../images/image.png

== Files ==
A utility class which offers methods to manage files/directories
+ Create, copy, move, delete, read, write
+ Verify permissions, attributes etc.

== Normalization ==
Used to remove redundant elements from the path, like "." (actual path) and ".." (parent directory)
+ Simplify and standardize the path
Ex:
home\renzo\dev\..\..\file.txt -> home\file.txt
or
\home\.\renzo\.\dev -> \home\renzo\dev

== Relativization ==
The relativization returns the relative path from two paths
Ex:
/home/renzo -> /home/renzo/devdojo/HelloWorld.java = devdojo\HelloWorld.java
/home/renzo -> /usr/local = ..\..\usr\local
temp -> temp/temp.20212023 = temp.20212023
The paths need to be of the same type (absolutes or relatives), or will throw exception

== BasicFileAttributes ==
Give attributes about directories/files
+ BasicFileAttributes -> For general systems
Implements BasicFileAttributes:
+ DosFileAttributes -> destined for Windows
+ PosixFileAttributes -> destined for Unix OS
